# 6. Your Own Runtime

This is another fundamental component.

Your programming language needs something that **executes it**.

Think:

```text
YOUR LANGUAGE
       ↓
 YOUR RUNTIME
       ↓
 ACTUAL APPLICATION
```

Your runtime interprets what your language says and produces the actual functioning application.

For example:

```text
BUTTON "Login"
ACTION LOGIN
```

Your runtime knows what `LOGIN` means.

It connects the UI to your authentication system.

The user never needs to write:

```javascript
